{"name":"Black Market","hex":"#222244","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black market","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Trade that is in violation of restrictions, rationing, or price controls.","The people who engage in such trade, or that sector of the economy."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To sell (goods) on the black market.","To take part in black-market trading."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black_market"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black market","blocks":[{"text":"A black market is a clandestine market or series of transactions that has some aspect of illegality within a legal jurisdiction; it may also not be compliant with an institutional set of rules. If the rule defines the set of goods and services whose production and distribution are prohibited or restricted by law, non-compliance with the rule constitutes a black-market trade since the transaction itself is illegal. Such transactions include the illegal drug trade, prostitution, illegal currency transactions, and human trafficking."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Black_market_in_Shinbashi.JPG/330px-Black_market_in_Shinbashi.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_market"},{"title":"Black Market (Rick Ross album)","blocks":[{"text":"Black Market is the eighth studio album by American rapper Rick Ross. The album was released on December 4, 2015, by Maybach Music Group and Def Jam Recordings. The album features guest appearances from John Legend, CeeLo Green, Nas, DJ Premier, Mariah Carey, Mary J. Blige, Chris Brown, Future and The-Dream."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/10/Rick_Ross_Black_Market.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Market_(Rick_Ross_album)"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/15-10-27-Vista_des_de_l%27est%C3%A0tua_de_Colom_a_Barcelona-WMA_2834.jpg/500px-15-10-27-Vista_des_de_l%27est%C3%A0tua_de_Colom_a_Barcelona-WMA_2834.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/15-10-27-Vista_des_de_l%27est%C3%A0tua_de_Colom_a_Barcelona-WMA_2834.jpg/1280px-15-10-27-Vista_des_de_l%27est%C3%A0tua_de_Colom_a_Barcelona-WMA_2834.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/15-10-27-Vista_des_de_l%27est%C3%A0tua_de_Colom_a_Barcelona-WMA_2834.jpg/500px-15-10-27-Vista_des_de_l%27est%C3%A0tua_de_Colom_a_Barcelona-WMA_2834.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illegal street traders in Barcelona in 2015","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A15-10-27-Vista_des_de_l'est%C3%A0tua_de_Colom_a_Barcelona-WMA_2834.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Mercado_Negro%2C_La_Paz%2C_Bolivia.JPG/500px-Mercado_Negro%2C_La_Paz%2C_Bolivia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pars